{
  "version": 1,
  "source": "Travian: Legends published unit tables",
  "$comment": [
    "Travian's own tribes, transcribed. These numbers are not ours to balance:",
    "players know them by heart and every combat calculator on the internet",
    "assumes them, so scripts/validate-canon.js fails the build if a tribe file",
    "drifts off them and scripts/rebuild-troop-tables.js copies rather than",
    "generates them.",
    "",
    "Stats are BASE values at smithy level 0. Beware the official support.travian",
    "comparison table, which publishes level-20 upgraded values — it lists a",
    "Legionnaire at 52.4 attack where the base figure is 40.",
    "",
    "Travian gives each tribe ten units and our roster has eleven slots, so every",
    "canonical tribe has exactly one 'extension' slot that is ours to invent.",
    "Those are marked separately and are held, by the same validator, to sitting",
    "alongside the published units rather than outclassing them.",
    "",
    "Units carry a cost only where the published figure has been verified;",
    "where it has not, the slot is priced by our own model from the real stats.",
    "Wildlife has no published price at all because it cannot be trained."
  ],
  "sources": {
    "roman": [
      "answers.travian.com aid=150-159 via web.archive.org (official, 'value at troop level 0')",
      "travian.kirilloid.ru/js/units.js T4.6",
      "support.travian.com/en/articles/187 (level-20 table, back-solved to base)"
    ],
    "teuton": [
      "answers.travian.com aid=162-171 via web.archive.org (official, base values)",
      "travian.kirilloid.ru/js/units.js T4.6",
      "support.travian.com/en/articles/187 (level-20 table, back-solved to base)"
    ],
    "gaul": [
